+- AD-12 (inherited, superseded by AD-14) Helper modules are pure, argument-checking functions that stand alone: the paging helper and the text helpers are not used by the server today and only their tests call them, and the paging helper reports the page, the page count and the items but not the list length or the size. Why: the README lists them as separate modules beside the server and states no use for them (inferred). Evidence: `src/paginate.js` `paginate`; `src/strings.js` `capitalize`; `test/paginate.test.js` "paginate returns the requested page of an evenly divided list". Basis: S5.
